    "narrative": "With SB scarcity dictating our aggressive stance, **Bryce Harper** (78.57) and **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) emerge as the anchor points of today\u2019s lineup. **Bryce Harper** draws a prime matchup against R. Johnson, whose 5.16 xERA represents the softest target on the slate, and we are capitalizing on the favorable SP skill gap to vault him to the top of our daily efficiency rankings. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a 10% park boost at home against Baz, with his dynamic platoon advantage providing the necessary upside to push him into elite territory. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a must-start at 72.47; while Lynch IV presents a neutral challenge, the consistent production from **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** in the #3 hole remains our most reliable floor.\n\nWe are hunting efficiency against weak arms, specifically targeting the Johnson matchup. **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02) both receive massive boosts from the SP skill differential, with **Jung Hoo Lee** further aided by favorable wind conditions pushing his profile into the high-60s. The most difficult decision rested on the bench, where **Gleyber Torres** (55.46) nearly cracked the starting nine. Ultimately, while **Gleyber Torres** possesses an appealing platoon edge against the lefty Snell, the 15% penalty applied for Snell's strikeout profile makes the risk of a capped-game start unfavorable compared to the steady output of **Dylan Beavers** or **Braden Montgomery**. \n\nManagers should note that we are operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key pieces, including **Bryce Harper**, **Luis Arraez**, and **Justin Crawford**. While **Justin Crawford** is projected at a solid 63.67, his score is depressed by an assumed #9 batting position; should he shift up the order, his utility as an elite speed threat becomes even more vital to our league-wide standing. We have opted to bench **Daulton Varsho** and **JJ Bleday** to prioritize hitters with cleaner platoon matchups, specifically shielding our roster from the elite-level arm of Gausman, who effectively neutralized **JJ Bleday**\u2019s upside in our final optimization pass.",
